Z||000000||FieroRacer||09-27-2001||04:48 PM||||I have a 85 GT and I cannot take the absurd oil pan out!!!  I've gotten as far as getting all the bolts off and watching the oil pan sit on exhaust and motor mount.  Anyone have any advice?||||reg||8
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||09-27-2001||07:30 PM||||You will need to search thru the archives.This suject has been raised many times in the past I dont Know what the trick is as I have not had the pleasure of removing my oil pan yet.||||reg||4
Z||000002||FieroRacer||09-27-2001||07:46 PM||||You're lucky||||reg||9
Z||000003||87GTZ34||09-27-2001||08:06 PM||||Racer, I have an '87 which the pan and front cover are a slightly different configuration.  I think they come out the same way though.  I dropped the exhaust down and removed the front (of the engine) bracket.  You have to support the engine of course.  I think others have done it different ways but that was the fastest for me. GL||||reg||1
Z||000004||varnster||09-27-2001||10:19 PM||||yea you have to take loose the pass, front engine mount,and support the engine with a bottle jack on that side, also remove the starter. archives will explain it all, good<BR>luck! pulling that pan is no fun I feel for<BR>you.<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000005||2farnorth||09-28-2001||06:08 AM||||My manual says to take off the alternator and its lower support, loosen the a/c compressor and move it aside, loosen the 2<BR>motor mount bolts. Raise the pass side of the eng enough to clear the 2 mount bolts.<BR>Remove the mount bracket, starter, and the transmission dust shield.  Oh, forgot the dogbone on the top side.  Take one end of it off before you raise the engine.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||TooManyFieros||09-28-2001||02:32 PM||||I find it easy to drop the whole thing on the floor. Then you can get at anything you want and I'll bet you already have more time in it then it takes to drop out the whole cradle out.||||reg||6
Z||000007||TooManyFieros||09-28-2001||02:32 PM||||I find it easy to drop the whole thing on the floor. Then you can get at anything you want and I'll bet you already have more time in it then it takes to drop out the whole cradle out.||||reg||6
